NEEDS RUSSELL SIGN-OFF. Do not apply without that sign-off.

A time-locked lock note is the principal. withdraw() still pays that
principal out as a receipt. The note stays an admit leaf, and
lockNoteSpendRejected does not refuse a spend of it once the tranche
has been dropped. Refuse the withdraw when any matured tranche is
noteIsPrincipal. The owner spends the unlocked note and claims the
reward. A plain lock receipt, which is not a note, can still withdraw.

The other minimal shape is to make the two mutually exclusive: a
withdraw nullifies the lock note's spend, and an unlocked note refuses
the withdraw. Refusal is the smaller change. It belongs in withdraw()
and in verifyReservePayout, so apply and the pre-check agree.
boundReserveWithdraw does not see tranches. After this patch a
full-epoch time-locked withdraw still passes that coarser cap, then
fails in the vault trial with note_principal.

